  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    The Vum∴tenebra was the conflagration at Terrace Momiou, a contested trade-hub in the Nightshelf's upper reaches, during which ☽'shadow Covens' Order — the dominant Nightshelf religious-military faction — deployed the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral against a population aligned with the E'frostlings, a merchant faction controlling fire-core trade. The fighting shattered the Flipper Accord, the trade compact binding Aurora Stack and Nightshelf, and fractured the Nightshelf's internal order for a generation. It was fought during the Faction Wars. The Order classified it as 'reclamation of contested fire-core assets.' The Nightshelf remembers it as war.
    
    ## The Fighting
    
    The conflict began when the Order unearthed an unspecified relic at Terrace Momiou — no surviving source identifies it clearly. What followed was the first confirmed internal deployment of the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, a Nightshelf magic capable of fracturing time and memory within ice, against a Nightshelf-aligned civilian population. At least three of the five known Spiral practitioners participated.
    
    The Spiral's preservation properties compounded the killing. Fire-deaths were sealed into crystalline memory-structures and recycled across seasons — victims trapped burning repeatedly through the ice's own recall. Tunnel systems were frozen mid-collapse. E'frostling guild-members drowned in flooded chambers while retreating. Seventeen were killed and struck from guild registers, their fire-core allocations redistributed.
    
    The figure seventeen appears in Fire Keeper interment records. The Foundation ice preserves sixteen thermal cessations in the relevant stratum, with two signatures redistributed into the Profun∴lapsum casualty rolls. The discrepancy is one body. I no longer have staff to send down to recount.
    
    The Holdborn (ice-thresh), a splinter faction of the E'frostlings, arrived after the fighting had ended. Survivors bear geometric frost-scarring that luminesces near active fire-cores — a permanent mark of exposure. ☽'visois' Mask, the shadow-steel artifact later carried by multiple wielders, took the crack along its left cheekbone during the violence. It was never repaired.
    
    ## Consequences
    
    The crystal stockpiles destroyed at Terrace Momiou rendered the Flipper Accord inoperable. Seven subsequent renegotiations produced casualties at each round. The Order invoked Foedus∴vincu provisions — the Nightshelf's de facto constitutional charter — as legal justification. No witness agreed to testify under Lex∴andatum protections to challenge the invocation. The E'frostlings eventually claimed the surface, but the cost was written in ice-memory and carved into memorial stones that no one visits.
    
    In the aftermath, the Order conducted experimental work beneath the Terrace, attempting to fuse aurora-light with captured flame into a self-sustaining fire-core. The fused core held for three days before developing autonomous hunger. Fourteen fire-keepers died in containment efforts. The site was sealed beneath the eastern spire, its existence suppressed under the Long-dark Edict. Later accounts confirm a corrupted fire-core remained buried there, spreading taint through the Order's own structures for years afterward.
    
    ## Commemoration
    
    Four memorial laws were enacted: Foedus∴vincu, Memoria∴moria, Mandatum∴absconditu, and Mandatum∴ccord. The Nightshelf does not speak their names aloud. Watchers of undetermined nature were reported in the tunnels around Terrace Momiou in subsequent weeks; no archive recorded what they were. Kael, whose entire bloodline perished there, still leaves fire-core offerings at the Terrace's frozen edge. No one asks why.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579888276_0", anchor: "Seven subsequent renegotiations produced casualties at each round.", text: "Three of these renegotiations occurred in secret before the public version was signed. I found the drafts frozen in administrative ice — different hands, different strata, one bearing a thermal signature consistent with Nightshelf diplomatic seals that were retired before the Faction Wars officially ended. The public record counts seven. The ice counts ten. Whether the secret rounds are a subset of the seven or additional to them is the single most consequential unresolved question in Flipper Accord scholarship, and I have raised it in three separate filings to the Council. No response. The commission that appointed me has been dissolved. The commission that replaced it does not appear to know the drafts exist.", type: :correction, display: :full
